The files under upstream/ are unmodified copies identified in upstream.lock.json.
LICENSE and upstream/LICENSE preserve the upstream license text.
Bundled third-party components retain their own licenses as recorded below.

skills/modernize/SKILL.md, the stage references, and the Copilot command and
specialist instructions adapt the upstream entry, review, brief, transform,
verification, business-rule extraction, test-engineer and architecture-critic
approaches. Changes for this port include native Copilot chat, conversational
continuation, project setup discovery, adapter review and lifecycle checks,
explicit evidence limitations, and Playwright BDD legacy baselines with current
source/test/environment evidence checks. File-level notices distinguish these
adaptations from the added runtime, evidence and capture guidance. The port
preserves upstream review/brief artifact conventions while adapting routine
approvals, questions, scoped candidate verification and client tool names to native chat.
The status guidance and optional report follow the upstream saved-artifact
overview approach. scripts/build_report.py is a new implementation for this
port's artifacts; it does not implement upstream proof verdicts.
assets/report/report.html combines local presentation with content sections
adapted from the pinned upstream HTML report. assets/report/diagrams.js adapts
its diagram renderer. Recorded proof results remain saved evidence, not a new
computation or human acceptance.
scripts/inventory.py wraps the unmodified upstream sharder and adds file hashes,
selection identity, HTML/HTM source selection, and a read-only JSON interface.

The discovery artifact validator, native result, baseline and candidate evidence
checkers, and consumer documentation are additions to this port.
This project does not imply endorsement by Anthropic, GitHub, or the Guardian.

The 0.4.0 port also adapts preflight, assessment, mapping, extraction, uplift,
reimagine and hardening, with native Copilot specialist profiles. The original
comparison, baseline, rule-tracing, uplift and proof helpers are bundled unchanged.
scripts/upstream_checks.py dispatches those helpers and adapts existing R-prefixed
rule IDs and optional prepared-source snapshots without rewriting saved records.
Claude UI hooks, telemetry and Workflow execution are not included. All unchanged
imports are identified by path and hash in upstream.lock.json.

The E2E setup and scenario-quality guidance uses original wording informed by
the Guardian Agentsy E2E playbook and feature-files practices. The reviewed
e2e-test-setup and feature-files plugin.json manifests name Guardian News & Media
as author and declare Apache-2.0. This package retains that attribution and the
Apache 2.0 license.
